<title>UK: Southern Co prices $325 million 40-year bond.</title>
<headline>Southern Co prices $325 million 40-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been priced and increased to $325 million from $300 million, joint lead managers Lehman and Goldman Sachs International said.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SOUTHERN COMPANY CAPITAL TRUST 1</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  SOUTHERN COMPANY</p>
<p> AMT    $300 MLN	COUPON     8.19	MATURITY    01.FEB.37</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS/REOFF  PAR	 PAY DATE   S03.FEB.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.00	LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  A3/A-     DENOMS (K) =	   SPREAD	+125 BP</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 30-YEAR U.S TREASURY</p>
<p> NOTES	CALLABLE AT PAR IN 2007. S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>		SUBORDINATED CAPITAL INCOME SECURITIES DEAL</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
